Hi fellow Smugmuggers.  Here's my post for tonight.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
September 13, 2010&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Not the best of quality - but a fun pic.  We were at the car &amp; vintage air show weekend before last.  I thought it looked best in Sepia tones.  &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
We took our Grandson Benjamin (in the front of the picture - he is 2 years old) and our other Grandson Case (he's 4 years old) that's sitting behind brother Benjamin.  &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Grandpa (see him at the top of the photo)  took the two of them onto the huge Chinook helicopter - they were so excited that they were just shaking with happiness.  &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
These two boys were sitting in the &quot;big people's seat&quot;  (e.g. the pilot's seat)  of the helicopter. They were so excited and talked about it all day.  &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
But then again - grandpa was pretty excited too.  &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Grandma (me) was trying to get good shots &amp; only had the macro lens with me - so it wasn't the best of shots.  But it was just so cool to see how excited these little boys were with all the WWI, WWII, Korea and Vietnam planes on the ground &amp; flying overhead.  &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
They were just thrilled and chattering all day long.  They paid little or no attention to the classic cars (including Grandma's &amp; Grandpa's cars) that were there beside the planes.  They were all about the airplanes. &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
 What a fun day we had!&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Aren't grandkids fun?&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Have a great evening!!!&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Linda
